%T A394665 26,28,29,29,29,29,30,33,35,36,36,36,36,38,40,42,43,42,40,42,45,47,49,
%U A394665 50,50,50,50,52,54,56,56,57,57,57,59,61,63,64,64,64,64,65,65,69
%N A394665 a(n) is the number of distinct nonzero eigenvalues of the n X n matrix M with M(i,j) = 1 if |i-j| <= 3 and M(i,j) = 0 otherwise.
%C A394665 M is the adjacency matrix of the cube of the path graph P_n with a loop at every vertex.
%C A394665 a(n) is also the minimal order of a linear recurrence with constant coefficients satisfied, for k >= 1, by the number of base-n circular k-digit numbers with adjacent digits differing by 3 or less; that count equals trace(M^k). Writing trace(M^k) = Sum_{L} m_L * L^k over the distinct eigenvalues L of M with algebraic multiplicities m_L > 0, no term can cancel, and the zero eigenvalues contribute nothing for k >= 1, so the minimal order is exactly the number of distinct nonzero eigenvalues. This is proved, not empirical.
%C A394665 Consequently a(n) gives the minimal recurrence order for A124999 (n=5), A125316 (n=6), ..., A125342 (n=32). In those entries a(0) = 1 is the empty-word convention and lies outside the range of the recurrence.
%C A394665 The sequence is not monotonic: a(8) = 8 but a(9) = 7, and a(43) = 43 but a(45) = 40, reflecting coincidences among the eigenvalues.
%H A394665 Rafał Wiktorowicz, <a href="/A394665/b394665.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..316</a>
%F A394665 a(n) = deg(q) - deg(gcd(q, q')), where q(x) is the characteristic polynomial of M with all factors of x removed; i.e., the number of distinct roots of the nonzero part of the characteristic polynomial.
%e A394665 For n = 17 the minimal order is 15, so A125327 satisfies a linear recurrence of order 15 and no linear recurrence of smaller order.
%Y A394665 Cf. A124999, A125316, A125317, A125318, A125319, A125320, A125321, A125322, A125323, A125324, A125325, A125326, A125327, A125328, A125329, A125330, A125331, A125332, A125333, A125334, A125335, A125336, A125337, A125338, A125339, A125340, A125341, A125342.
